From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 21:46:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1076/3799] soh: rename D_801755D8 -> gUnusedAudioValues

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: the in-tree comment on its declaration reads "// unused"; three s32 slots with no reader.
Defined in soh/src/code/audio_init_params.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/audio_init_params.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/audio_init_params.c b/soh/src/code/audio_init_params.c
index b01d44a20..80cf8fce5 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/audio_init_params.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/audio_init_params.c
@@ -4,7 +4,8 @@
 u8 gUnusedAudioBuffer[0xA0]; // unused, was D_8016F0E0 [LLM:HIGH]
 AudioContext gAudioContext;
 void (*D_801755D0)(void);
-s32 D_801755D8[3]; // unused
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was D_801755D8: the in-tree comment on its declaration reads "// unused"; three s32 slots with no reader.
+s32 gUnusedAudioValues[3]; // unused, was D_801755D8 [LLM:HIGH]
 
 const s16 D_8014A6C0[] = {
     0x1C00, // unused
